      body: "The Prado house in Jardim Botânico was still the same. The same green gate that creaked, the same jabuticaba tree in the yard, the same dog, Paçoca, now fatter and grayer, who recognized you at once and threw himself against your legs.\n\n— Traitor — you said, scratching his ear. — You didn't even give me time to get nervous.\n\nHelena herself opened the kitchen door. Hair shorter, at the jaw. A linen blouse the color of sand. The same perfume of orange and some wood you never learned the name of.\n\n— Marina. — She smiled carefully. — Thank you for saying yes.\n\n— Thank you for asking.\n\nA second of silence. The kind that weighs.\n\n— The kitchen is all yours — she said, finally. — I changed very little. My mother is at the salon getting her hair done. She arrives at seven. The guests at eight.\n\n— And Caio?\n\n— Sleeping. He's twenty-seven and he still sleeps until three on a Saturday afternoon.\n\nYou laughed. So did she. And it was so easy to laugh with her that you got angry at yourself.\n\nTeté arrived right after, carrying the coolers and talking loud:\n\n— Good afternoon, family! Where's the bathroom? I drank a whole mate on the way.\n\nHelena pointed down the hall. As Teté passed, she looked at you and mouthed, with no sound: \"she's beautiful, huh\". You pretended not to see.",
