        title: "First Page",
        flower: "Coffee in Leblon",
        body: "Meanwhile you and Teté redid the bakery. You sanded walls, chose tile, fought with suppliers. Helena sent the blue folder back, with a note: \"Use whatever you want. I'm happy from far away.\" You kept the folder with care, but you drew your house yourself.\n\nBia came back on opening day. She arrived at the glass of the big window, camera at her neck, and stayed outside, watching you cook, before she came in. Then she came in and photographed the whole night: Dona Lúcia crying over the duck rice, Caio holding Davi's hand, Teté opening the sparkling wine with her teeth.\n\nFor the last photo of the night she asked Caio to take it: the two of you at the counter, laughing, an apron and a green dress.\n\n— This one goes on the wall — she said.\n\n— The restaurant's?\n\n— Our house's. Someday. When it's time.\n\nThe next Sunday you went together to the market in Glória. The persimmon man saw you coming and folded his arms.\n\n— Here comes the salad woman.\n\n— This time there are two — Bia said.",
