      music: "despedida",
      body: "Teté answered shouting, because she was at the market.\n\n— Talk, chef!\n\n— I want the bakery.\n\nSilence in the whole market. Or at least that was how it seemed.\n\n— Say it again — she said.\n\n— I want the bakery. I want to open it with you. I'm going to tell Rodrigo no. And I am not going to start anything with anyone now, Teté. Not with Helena. Not with Bia. I spent a year and a half waiting for someone to tell me who I was. I want to find out by myself.\n\nOn the other end, a can hit the floor and someone apologized.\n\n— I dropped the condensed milk — Teté said, crying. — It's worth it. It's so worth it.\n\nYou called Helena after that, and Bia right after. Both calls were short and honest. Helena said: \"It's the most beautiful choice you could have made.\" Bia said: \"I'll be the first customer. Or the second, because Dona Lúcia is going to get there first.\" They were both right.\n\nYou called Rodrigo last.\n\n— No, again? — he said.\n\n— No. But this time it's a no with a yes inside it.\n\nHe laughed and asked you to hold a table for the opening.\n\nThe months after that were the most exhausting of your life, and the happiest. You and Teté sanded walls, chose green-and-white tile, and learned to light an old wood-fired oven with the help of a man of eighty who had been the baker there. You went back to writing menus in a notebook, in the small hours, with cold coffee.",
